// =============================================================================
// Rent to Own — Business Operating Systems from the Store Floor
// =============================================================================
// Darrell, 2026-09-17, two spoken directives. First: "I would like to have a
// whole business suite of courses... use rent to own business models as a
// foundation for inventory control, sales, collections, customer service,
// marketing. So go research rent to own stores and how they operate." Then the
// correction that decided the course's name and its spine: "use the term RENT
// TO OWN. So renting something to own it because I've worked for Rentway first
// and Rentway taught me way more than Rent-A-Center BECAUSE OF THE WAY THAT
// BUSINESS OPERATING SYSTEMS WORKED... it taught me how to understand business
// flow." And the ladder: "I started out as an account manager, went from an
// account manager to an assistant manager, from an assistant manager to the
// general manager. I WORKED IN EVERY SINGLE POSITION."
//
// So this is not a course about a company. It is a course about an OPERATING
// SYSTEM, taught by a man who sat in every seat of it, with the Word above it.
//
// THE SPINE IS HIS, NOT BORROWED. Four of his own teachings run through every
// lesson: honor as the operating principle ("the only time you have any sort of
// friction is when honor's left the room"), COVENANT OVER CONTRACT ("a covenant
// from Yahweh is way better... contracts, people can break them"), his Uncle
// Russell's maxim ("Put your head down and go get the information. Always come
// out of there with the information... the understanding... the skills"), and
// the closing standard ("you want to be the best in everything you're doing.
// BE THE BEST IN THIS TOO").
//
// PROVENANCE, AND THE TWO TIERS (DR-0076 / DR-0100). The operating facts here
// are carried from primary and industry sources and are labelled as such in the
// prose: the on-rent / held-for-rent split and the income-forecasting method
// from Rent-A-Center's own SEC filings; the agreement's terminability and the
// return-and-owe-nothing feature from the FTC; the early-purchase-option saving
// and that roughly three agreements in four end in a voluntary return from the
// industry association (APRO); the account manager's own job definition from
// the role as the industry posts it. The Rent-Way acquisition figures (784
// stores in 34 states, about $567 million, completed 15 November 2006) are as
// Rent-A-Center announced them. Every KJV line was FETCHED from
// app/public/bible/kjv this session and is quoted verbatim; the course gate
// asserts each quoted span against the corpus, so a drifted quote fails CI.
//
// AND THE JUST WEIGHT IS NOT SKIPPED. The FTC's established finding is that
// rent-to-own total cost "can be two to three times retail prices, and
// sometimes more." That is stated plainly (DR-0100: under-claiming a verified
// truth is as much a failure of truth as over-claiming) and weighed against the
// just weight the Word commands — while the operating discipline is taught as
// genuinely excellent, because those are two different things and a man can run
// the first with real excellence while the second is being weighed. Lesson 2
// holds both, and holds them apart.
// =============================================================================
