    lesson: `THE SEAT YOU ARE IN, AND EVERY SEAT ABOVE IT. This course is taught from inside the building, not from outside it. The man teaching it started as an ACCOUNT MANAGER, went from account manager to ASSISTANT MANAGER, and from assistant manager to GENERAL MANAGER. He worked every single position, and he says there is a story and a narrative about every single one of those roles, because Yahweh taught him something through every season of his life. Keep that word SEASON. It is the reason this lesson comes first.

WHY THE OPERATING SYSTEM IS THE SUBJECT AND THE COMPANY IS NOT. He worked at Rentway first, and Rentway taught him more than the larger company did - not because of its sign, but BECAUSE OF THE WAY ITS BUSINESS OPERATING SYSTEMS WORKED. Those systems were good enough that a young man could learn BUSINESS FLOW from them: where a thing enters, what happens to it, who touches it, what it costs while it waits, and how it leaves. That is what an operating system is, and that is what this course teaches. A company can be bought, renamed or closed. A working operating system, once you can see it, you keep.

THE FIRST SEAT IS NOT THE SMALL SEAT. In a rent-to-own store the account manager is the seat closest to the customer: the deliveries, the pickups, the phone, the doorstep, the early conversation when an account slips. It is often treated as the entry job. The Word treats it as the test of everything above it: "He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much: and he that is unjust in the least is unjust also in much." (Luke 16:10). Read that as an operating fact and not a sentiment. Nothing about a man changes when his title changes. The general manager's integrity is the account manager's integrity, promoted. If the small seat was worked carelessly, the big seat is carelessness with more authority.

AND THE PROMOTION RUNS THAT WAY IN THE WORD TOO: "His lord said unto him, Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord." (Matthew 25:21). FAITHFUL OVER A FEW THINGS FIRST. That is the whole ladder in one sentence, and it is why working every seat is not a detour on the way to the office - it IS the qualification.

THE STANDARD IN THE SEAT, WHOEVER IS WATCHING. "And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men;" (Colossians 3:23). "Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might; for there is no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest." (Ecclesiastes 9:10). And the Word is not shy about where that leads: "Seest thou a man diligent in his business? he shall stand before kings; he shall not stand before mean men." (Proverbs 22:29). Diligence in business is not a worldly ambition the Word tolerates. It is a thing the Word NOTICES.

WHY IT IS BEING POURED OUT NOW. The teacher's own words: the Lord says you are to love Him with your whole mind, will, soul and emotion - every aspect of who you are as a human. "And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment." (Mark 12:30). So at this point in life the work is to pour out the knowledge, wisdom and understanding already gathered, as much as possible and as humbly as possible - to GIVE AWAY AS MUCH AS HE CAN BEFORE HE PASSES. He looks at that as feeding sheep, and the Word gives that its name three times over: "He saith unto him, Feed my lambs." (John 21:15); "He saith unto him, Feed my sheep." (John 21:16); "Jesus saith unto him, Feed my sheep." (John 21:17). Peter was asked three times whether he loved Him, and each answer was met with the same instruction. FEEDING IS WHAT LOVE WAS TOLD TO DO.

WHO THIS IS FOR. The people in the body who would love to comprehend what the King says and are willing to spend time processing what He is saying. People who want A SOUND MIND: "For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind." (2 Timothy 1:7). In the teacher's words - people who do not want a lot of stress, but who are willing to get in and get some stress, because there is work to do. And yet peace is the point, because He is the Prince of Peace.

THE CLOSING STANDARD OF THE WHOLE COURSE. If something is off between what you are doing and what the King says in the Word, it makes no sense not to fall in line with what He is saying. His own comparison: it is like being in the military and skipping the exercises - left, left, right, left - and then wondering why nothing works. You want to be the best at everything you do. BE THE BEST IN THIS TOO. Business is not the part of life where the standard drops.`,
